    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Grouped by slice and mode, deliberately not by queue: a broadcast subscription's queue is named amq.gen-… and is regenerated on every connection, so grouping by it produces a fresh legend entry per reconnect and no series that lasts a day. bus_events_failed_total has no series at all until the first nack, so an empty 'nacked' legend means nothing has failed — not that nothing is measured. See the counter beside this panel. This is also not a dead-letter count: x-delivery-limit moves a message to <queue>.quarantine without telling the adapter, so a transient failure on its fifth delivery is counted here exactly like its first.",
