    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Cumulative since the exporter started, deliberately NOT increase(...[1h]). Measured: two poison nacks had happened and the windowed form read 0 — Prometheus cannot see the rise of a counter whose first sample is already non-zero, and a series born mid-window is the normal case here, not an edge, because these are push-interval samples from a service that restarts often. A green zero in a box labelled 'nacked' while deliveries were failing is the exact lie this dashboard exists to prevent. It resets when the service does, which is visible as a step down rather than a wrong number. Zero here is still a real zero: bus_events_failed_total has no series until the first nack and an absent series is not a zero, so the query falls back to vector(0) — honest only after a sum() with no `by`, since on a grouped query that would invent a series carrying no slice and no failure class, which is why it appears nowhere else here.",
